      "problem": "Identify the following surface: \n\n$$\n(x+2)^{2}-(y-1)^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <z<\\infty \n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1,\n$$\n\nand a hyperbolic cylinder, whose axis of symmetry is parallel to the $z$-axis and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ in the $xy$-plane, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-{x}_{0})^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-{y}_{0})^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder with the following parameters:\n\n$$\n({x}_{0},{y}_{0})=(-2,1),\\,a=b=1.\n$$",
